# Force LF line endings for shell scripts so they run correctly under
# GNU bash (e.g. inside the Docker build container). Windows core.autocrlf
# would otherwise rewrite them to CRLF, which breaks `make_cia.sh`
# (bash chokes on the trailing \r, so bannertool/-rsf args are dropped).
*.sh text eol=lf
*.rsf text eol=lf
# Normalize C/C++ sources to LF so the published tree stays clean regardless of
# the contributor's local core.autocrlf / editor. The local port history carries
# CRLF drift in many files; forcing LF here keeps `publish-master` diffs minimal.
*.c text eol=lf
*.h text eol=lf
